@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

# Run these top to bottom. Seats J5 and J6 are freed again by the last request (Cancel),
# so the whole file can be re-run. If you stop halfway, they free up on their own after 5 minutes.

### User 1 login: seeded user Arjun (expect 200 + token)
# @name user1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arjun@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### User 2 login: seeded user Priya, used to compete for the same seat (expect 200 + token)
# @name user2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### List events: we book seats on the first (soonest) upcoming event (expect 200)
# @name events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events?limit=1

### Hold 2 seats as user 1 with a fresh Idempotency-Key (expect 201, status "pending")
# @name hold
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/hold
Authorization: Bearer {{user1.response.body.token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{events.response.body.$.data[0]._id}}",
  "seatLabels": ["J5", "J6"]
}

### Repeat the same hold with the SAME Idempotency-Key, like a client retrying after a timeout (expect 200, same _id as above, no new booking)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/hold
Authorization: Bearer {{user1.response.body.token}}
Idempotency-Key: {{hold.request.headers.Idempotency-Key}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{events.response.body.$.data[0]._id}}",
  "seatLabels": ["J5", "J6"]
}

### User 2 tries to hold a seat user 1 is holding (expect 409 "Seat J5 is no longer available")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/hold
Authorization: Bearer {{user2.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "{{events.response.body.$.data[0]._id}}",
  "seatLabels": ["J5"]
}

### Confirm as user 1: simulated payment, held seats become booked (expect 200, status "confirmed"; 409 if 5 minutes have passed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{hold.response.body._id}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{user1.response.body.token}}

### My bookings as user 1: newest first, with event and seat details (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/me
Authorization: Bearer {{user1.response.body.token}}

### Cancel as user 1: booking becomes "cancelled" and J5/J6 are available again (expect 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{hold.response.body._id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{user1.response.body.token}}
